(subclass InsufficientSpecificationBug SoftwareBug)
(termFormat EnglishLanguage InsufficientSpecificationBug "insufficient specification bug")
(documentation InsufficientSpecificationBug EnglishLanguage "A &%SoftwareBug
whose discriminating property is that a &%ContentBearingObject records the
specifying agent's &%intendedBehavior for the program, and a different agent
reading the same document derives a different &%intendedBehavior for the same
program.  The document admits two readings; the spec is therefore
insufficient to constrain the implementation.  Adapted from CWE-1059
(Insufficient Technical Documentation) and IEEE 29148-2018 5.2.5
('unambiguous' quality characteristic).")

(=>
  (and
    (instance ?PROG ComputerProgram)
    (programBehavior ?PROG ?INPUT ?ACTUAL)
    (intendedBehavior ?PROG ?INTENDED ?AGENT)
    (not (equal ?ACTUAL ?INTENDED))
    (exists (?DOC ?AGENT2 ?INTENDED2)
      (and
        (instance ?DOC ContentBearingObject)
        (containsInformation ?DOC (intendedBehavior ?PROG ?INTENDED ?AGENT))
        (instance ?AGENT2 AutonomousAgent)
        (not (equal ?AGENT ?AGENT2))
        (believes ?AGENT2 (intendedBehavior ?PROG ?INTENDED2 ?AGENT))
        (not (equal ?INTENDED ?INTENDED2)))))
  (exists (?BUG)
    (and
      (instance ?BUG InsufficientSpecificationBug)
      (bugInProgram ?BUG ?PROG ?AGENT))))
